msiexec: parse the command line with the Windows rules, so a property value ending in a backslash survives

Windows' msiexec receives its command line from the caller (or from the shell) quoted according to
the documented rules, and the CRT turns it back into argv: quotes are delimiters and are removed,
and a run of backslashes in front of a quote is halved, with the quote still delimiting the
argument when their number is even and being taken literally when it is odd.  Wine's msiexec
replaces that with its own chomp() (programs/msiexec/msiexec.c), which kept the quotes in the
arguments it returned and had no backslash handling at all.

The AutoCAD 2027 installer is what runs into this.  For every package whose install directory is
under "C:\Program Files\..." it passes the install location with a trailing backslash, e.g.

  msiexec /i ...\x64\acadprivate\acadprivate.msi /qn MSIFASTINSTALL=7 ARPSYSTEMCOMPONENT=1
          INSTALLDIR=C:\Program Files\Autodesk\AutoCAD 2027\ REBOOT=ReallySuppress ADSK_ODIS_SETUP=1

Wine's loader (build_command_line in dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c) quotes that argument and doubles the
trailing backslash, as the Windows rules require, so the Windows command line is well-formed:

  "...\msiexec.exe" /i ... "INSTALLDIR=C:\Program Files\Autodesk\AutoCAD 2027\\" /l*v ...

Old chomp() turned that back into the argument

  "INSTALLDIR=C:\Program Files\Autodesk\AutoCAD 2027\\"       (quotes kept, backslashes not halved)

build_properties() then took the text up to the '=' as the property name (so the name carried the
opening quote), found a value that already began with a quote and copied it verbatim, and handed
MsiInstallProductW

   ADSK_ODIS_SETUP=1 "INSTALLDIR="C:\Program Files\Autodesk\AutoCAD 2027\\""

msi_parse_command_line counted an odd number of quotes, warned "unbalanced quotes", returned
ERROR_INVALID_COMMAND_LINE and msiexec exited 103 with an MSI log that contains only its header -
no action of the package ever ran.  The same happens without the trailing backslash (the retained
quotes alone unbalance the property string), so every hand-run of these packages failed.
(Refuted along the way: the warning is not about Wine treating a backslash-prefixed quote as an
escaped quote - msi_parse_command_line only knows `"` - and the value parser is not the faulty
part; the malformed property string was produced by msiexec itself.)

Fix: chomp() now follows the Windows rules.  The callers that used to strip the quotes again
themselves (remove_quotes() on the package name, the log file and the DLL name) are unaffected,
because those arguments no longer carry the quotes, and the property arguments now reach
build_properties() the way Windows' msiexec sees them.

This is not the installer's own path: ODIS (install_manager) drives the packages through
MsiInstallProductW in-process and passes the value quoted
(`INSTALLDIR="C:\Program Files\Autodesk\AutoCAD 2027\"`), which the MSI command line parser already
handles - that path completes with the unpatched msi.dll.  The defect is confined to msiexec's own
argument marshalling, which is what the repair path and any hand-run of these packages uses.

Verified with acadprivate.msi (ADSK_ODIS_SETUP=1 satisfies its LaunchCondition), in a licensing
prefix so that its licensing custom actions pass:
  wine msiexec /i pkgs/x/x64/acadprivate/acadprivate.msi /qn 'ADSK_ODIS_SETUP=1'
               'INSTALLDIR=C:\Program Files\Autodesk\AutoCAD 2027\' /l*v msi.log
  before: exit 103, log = header only, `warn:msi:msi_parse_command_line unbalanced quotes`
  after:  exit 0, 93 "Action start" lines, INSTALL return value 1,
          Property(S): INSTALLDIR = C:\Program Files\Autodesk\AutoCAD 2027\,
          Property(S): LOCAL_INSTALLDIR = C:\Program Files\Autodesk\AutoCAD 2027, and the four
          payload files of the package in C:\Program Files\Autodesk\AutoCAD 2027 (the fifth one,
          MsiKeyFile_ACADLockSecuritySettings.dll, is conditioned on LOCKSECURITYSETTINGS=1,
          which the bundle leaves at 0 - as on the Windows guest)
No regression: without the trailing backslash and with an explicitly quoted path the property
value is parsed identically (`INSTALLDIR = C:\Program Files\Autodesk\AutoCAD 2027`).

--- a/programs/msiexec/msiexec.c
+++ b/programs/msiexec/msiexec.c
@@ -464,81 +464,82 @@
