 /*
- * state machine to break up the command line properly
+ * Break up the command line into arguments, using the same rules as the Windows command
+ * line parser: arguments are separated by spaces outside of quotes, quotes delimit an
+ * argument and are not part of it, and a run of backslashes in front of a quote is halved
+ * with the quote delimiting the argument when the number of backslashes is even, and with
+ * the quote being taken literally when that number is odd.  Note that msiexec is launched
+ * by other programs (and by the shell) with a command line that was quoted according to
+ * these rules, so e.g. a trailing backslash of an argument arrives doubled and must be
+ * halved again here, or the property value would not match what the caller passed.
  */
-
-enum chomp_state
-{
-    CS_WHITESPACE,
-    CS_TOKEN,
-    CS_QUOTE
-};
-
